.\" ###### Setup ############################################################
.Dd November 26, 2026
.Dt Reset\-Machine\-ID 1
.Os Reset\-Machine\-ID
.\" ###### Name #############################################################
.Sh NAME
.Nm Reset\-Machine\-ID
.Nd resets the machine identity state
.\" ###### Synopsis #########################################################
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm Reset\-Machine\-ID
.Op Fl H Ar hostname | Fl \-hostname Ar hostname
.br
.Op Fl M | Fl \-skip\-machine\-id
.br
.Op Fl S | Fl \-skip\-ssh\-configuration
.br
.Op Fl K | Fl \-skip\-ssh\-key\-replacement
.br
.Op Fl Z Ar zabbix\_server | Fl \-zabbix Ar zabbix\_server
.br
.Op Fl A | Fl \-install\-zabbix\-agent
.br
.Op Fl \-yes\-to\-all\-i\-am\-really\-sure
.Nm Reset\-Machine\-ID
.Op Fl h | Fl \-help
.Nm Reset\-Machine\-ID
.Op Fl v | Fl \-version
.\" ###### Description ######################################################
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm Reset\-Machine\-ID
resets the machine identity state, particularly for a cloned VM, to make it appear as a new machine.
Executing identity changes requires superuser (root) privileges.
It performs the following tasks:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
Change the system hostname, if a new one is provided
.Pq the Fl \-hostname No option
.It
Reset
.Pa /etc/machine\-id
and update
.Pa /var/lib/dbus/machine\-id
(symlink to
.Pa /etc/machine\-id )
.It
Reset the host ID in the Debian Popularity Contest configuration file, if installed
.It
Optionally install and configure Zabbix Agent for a given Zabbix server
.It
Provide hardened settings for the SSH client and server
.It
Back up existing SSH host keys and generate a new ED25519, ECDSA, and RSA key set
.El
.Pp
All modifications are confirmed interactively unless
.Fl \-yes\-to\-all\-i\-am\-really\-sure
is specified.
.\" ###### Arguments ########################################################
.Sh ARGUMENTS
The following options are available:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl H Ar hostname | Fl \-hostname Ar hostname
Set the given hostname (FQDN or short hostname) and update
.Pa /etc/hosts
accordingly.
.It Fl M | Fl \-skip\-machine\-id
Do not reset the machine ID.
.It Fl S | Fl \-skip\-ssh\-configuration
Do not make SSH configuration changes.
.It Fl K | Fl \-skip\-ssh\-key\-replacement
Do not replace SSH host keys.
.It Fl Z Ar zabbix\_server | Fl \-zabbix Ar zabbix\_server
Configure Zabbix Agent for the specified Zabbix server.
.It Fl A | Fl \-install\-zabbix\-agent
Install Zabbix Agent if no Zabbix Agent configuration is found when
.Fl Z
is given. On Debian and Ubuntu systems, this adds the official Zabbix APT repository (note that an official repository may not be available for every distribution release); on Fedora, openSUSE, Alpine, FreeBSD, NetBSD, and OpenBSD, the system package manager is used.
.It Fl \-yes\-to\-all\-i\-am\-really\-sure
Apply all requested hostname, machine\-ID, Zabbix Agent, SSH configuration, and SSH host\-key changes without interactive confirmation.
.It Fl h | Fl \-help
Prints the program's command\-line parameters and exits.
.It Fl v | Fl \-version
Prints the program version and exits.
.El
.\" ###### Files ############################################################
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /etc/machine\-id , /var/lib/dbus/machine\-id
System and D\-Bus machine identifier files.
.It Pa /etc/hosts , /etc/hostname , /etc/rc.conf , /etc/nodename
Hostname and local name\-resolution configuration files.
.It Pa /etc/ssh/ssh_config , /etc/ssh/sshd_config
OpenSSH client and daemon configuration files.
.It Pa /etc/zabbix/zabbix_agentd.conf , /etc/zabbix_agentd.conf
Zabbix Agent configuration files.
.El
.\" ###### Exit status ######################################################
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The
.Nm
tool exits with 0 on success, and >0 in case of an error.
.\" ###### Examples #########################################################
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -bullet
.It
sudo Reset\-Machine\-ID
.It
sudo Reset\-Machine\-ID \-\-yes\-to\-all\-i\-am\-really\-sure
.It
sudo Reset\-Machine\-ID \-\-hostname dbserver.domain.example
.It
sudo Reset\-Machine\-ID \-H server.domain.example \-Z zabbix.domain.example \-A
.It
sudo Reset\-Machine\-ID \-H server.domain.example \-\-zabbix zabbix.domain.example \-\-install\-zabbix\-agent
.It
sudo Reset\-Machine\-ID \-\-skip\-ssh\-configuration \-\-skip\-ssh\-key\-replacement
.It
Reset\-Machine\-ID \-\-help
.It
Reset\-Machine\-ID \-h
.It
Reset\-Machine\-ID \-\-version
.It
Reset\-Machine\-ID \-v
.El
